<h2>My Two Weeks at the Putney Columbia Climate School (Part 3)</h2>

<p class="date">August 2026</p>

<p>
As the final few days of the Putney Columbia Climate School approached, our focus shifted toward seeing climate action in practice, completing our Climate Action Projects, and reflecting on everything we had learned throughout the program. Looking back, these last few days were the perfect way to wrap up an unforgettable experience.
</p>

<h3>Day 10: Real-World Climate Solutions in Burlington</h3>

<p>
Day 10 took us on an excursion to Burlington, Vermont, where we explored how climate solutions are being implemented in the real world. Throughout the day, we visited several organizations and learned about different approaches to addressing environmental challenges.
</p>

<p>
One of the most interesting sessions focused on climate finance and entrepreneurship. We learned about Blue Forest, an organization that uses innovative financing to support environmental restoration projects. It was fascinating to see how investing in nature can create benefits not only for the environment but also for local communities.
</p>

