<p>
We also visited a company that collects waste from portable toilets and recycles urine into fertilizer. It definitely wasn't something I expected to learn about, but it showed how creative and unexpected climate solutions can be. It was a great reminder that sustainability can be found in places most people would never think to look.
</p>

<p>
After a full day of exploring Burlington, we had dinner together at Bread and Butter before heading back to campus. It was a nice way to reflect on everything we had learned throughout the day.
</p>

<h3>Day 11: Imagining a More Sustainable Future</h3>

<p>
Day 11 began with a lecture from Emma Kyzivat about creating just and sustainable futures. We discussed what a more sustainable world could look like and why climate solutions should not only protect the environment but also be fair and accessible for everyone.
</p>

<p>
After the lecture, we spent more time working on our Climate Action Projects as we prepared for our final presentations. It was exciting to see how much each project had developed since the beginning of the program and how everyone's ideas had continued to evolve.
</p>

<p>
Later that afternoon, we went berry picking, which gave us a chance to spend some time outdoors and enjoy Vermont's beautiful scenery. We ended the evening with field games, making it another day that balanced learning with time to relax and connect with everyone before the program came to an end.
</p>

