</section>

<p>
Later, we had our final biome meeting before gathering for the talent show, which was a fun way to celebrate everything we had accomplished together. That evening, we also had the privilege of hearing from Columbia Climate School Dean Alexis Abramson, whose keynote address was an inspiring way to conclude the academic portion of the program. Afterward, we enjoyed one final dinner together before attending the certificate ceremony.
</p>

<p>
For our last evening on campus, everyone stayed together for activities like karaoke and volleyball. It was the perfect way to spend our final night, making the most of our remaining time together before saying our goodbyes the next morning.
</p>

<h3>Looking Back</h3>

<p>
Looking back, attending the Putney Columbia Climate School was an experience I'll always be grateful for. Over the course of two weeks, I gained a much deeper understanding of climate science, policy, sustainability, and the many different ways people are working to address climate change. More importantly, the program showed me that meaningful action can happen at any age and that young people have an important role to play in shaping a more sustainable future.
</p>

<p>
Beyond everything I learned, I'll always remember the friendships I made, the conversations I had, and the memories we created together. I'm incredibly grateful to all of the experts, facilitators, counselors, and fellow students who made this experience so meaningful.
</p>

<p>
Thank you so much for following along with my journey through the Putney Columbia Climate School. I hope you enjoyed reading about my experience as much as I enjoyed sharing it. 🌿
</p>
